00:56:43.817 --> 00:56:45.597
I got you now, and I'm going to keep you.

1041
00:56:45.677 --> 00:56:48.357
Oh, sure you can keep me,
but what'll it get you?

1042
00:56:48.437 --> 00:56:50.057
You don't want me that way.

1043
00:56:50.837 --> 00:56:52.057
Oh, Echo,

1044
00:56:52.317 --> 00:56:56.297
wouldn't you rather have me liking you,
not thinking you were something mean and

1045
00:56:56.377 --> 00:56:58.537
cold-blooded like Herc and the Midge?

1046
00:56:58.617 --> 00:56:59.717
Wouldn't you rather have me...

1047
00:56:59.797 --> 00:57:05.617
have me strong for you, thankful
and alive, wanted to be with you?

1048
00:57:06.517 --> 00:57:10.017
That's a great line of chatter,
but it don't go with me.

1049
00:57:10.577 --> 00:57:13.197
Gee, you're a smart guy.

1050
00:57:13.277 --> 00:57:16.777
You were hot stuff for the near-sighted
old ladies in the parrots store.

1051
00:57:16.857 --> 00:57:20.377
But when it comes to doing something
decent, you're afraid to take the chance.

1052
00:57:20.457 --> 00:57:21.557
You're a yeller.

1053
00:57:21.637 --> 00:57:24.277
Hey, listen, you're trying to
pass the buck for me, ain't you?

1054
00:57:24.357 --> 00:57:26.837
So they'll get me in, you can hire him.

1055
00:57:27.817 --> 00:57:29.937
No, you don't love him.

1056
00:57:30.057 --> 00:57:31.877
All right, all right!

1057
00:57:31.957 --> 00:57:34.057
I do love him. I am in love with him.

1058
00:57:34.137 --> 00:57:36.997
I'll always love him. And if
you let him die, I'll hate you.

1059
00:57:37.077 --> 00:57:38.657
Do you hear me? I'll
hate the sight of you.

1060
00:57:38.737 --> 00:57:40.717
I'll lose you every time you touch me.

1061
00:57:40.797 --> 00:57:43.679
I'll be hoping every
minute that you'd vote dead!

1062
00:57:55.457 --> 00:58:00.617
I'll even take that from you,
Echo, if you'll do what I ask.

1063
00:58:05.077 --> 00:58:06.697
Did I...

1064
00:58:09.917 --> 00:58:11.897
I mean...

1065
00:58:19.917 --> 00:58:26.077
The utter futility of this attempt
at alibi and the positive discovery

1066
00:58:26.157 --> 00:58:30.877
of the stolen necklace concealed in
the room of the accused constitutes,

1067
00:58:30.957 --> 00:58:35.457
I think, ladies and gentlemen,
a plain case for conviction.

1068
00:58:36.757 --> 00:58:38.957
But you've told them that.

1069
00:58:39.037 --> 00:58:44.037
And I'm going to ask you to find
the defendant guilty of murder...

1070
00:58:44.117 --> 00:58:45.857
in the first degree.

1071
00:58:47.077 --> 00:58:49.237
Do you think they'll convict him?

1072
00:58:49.637 --> 00:58:51.257
He'll go to the chair.

1073
00:58:51.337 --> 00:58:52.717
It's a cinch.

1074
00:58:52.897 --> 00:58:57.537
Ladies and gentlemen, I have seldom
encountered a case where the facts are so

1075
00:58:57.617 --> 00:59:03.317
simple... and so self-evident as they
are in this case before us here today.

1076
00:59:03.797 --> 00:59:08.177
A murder has been committed and
some jewelry has been stolen.

1077
00:59:08.577 --> 00:59:11.717
There is no doubt about
the motive for the murder.

1078
00:59:11.797 --> 00:59:18.277
And there is no doubt that whoever stole
those jewels committed that hideous crime.

1079
00:59:18.977 --> 00:59:24.477
Now, the evidence has proved to you that
some of those jewels were found in the

1080
00:59:24.557 --> 00:59:26.457
possession of Hector McDonald.

1081
00:59:27.037 --> 00:59:31.657
Hector McDonald contends he knew nothing
about them or how they came into his

1082
00:59:31.737 --> 00:59:32.737
possession.

1083
00:59:32.817 --> 00:59:39.117
And his only defense is a vague
story about three people who

1084
00:59:39.197 --> 00:59:41.537
have mysteriously disappeared.

1085
00:59:41.757 --> 00:59:44.037
Who can they be?

1086
00:59:44.117 --> 00:59:50.537
Who are they? These three mysterious
people whom have so mysteriously

1087
00:59:50.617 --> 00:59:56.057
disappeared and the defense
cannot or dare not produce.

1088
00:59:58.657 --> 01:00:01.597
It is quite obvious, ladies and gentlemen,

1089
01:00:01.857 --> 01:00:07.457
that they are either accomplices to the
crime or else they are pure figments of

1090
01:00:07.537 --> 01:00:08.537
imagination.

1091
01:00:08.617 --> 01:00:13.997
We have heard a great deal today about the
fallibility of circumstantial evidence.

1092
01:00:14.217 --> 01:00:16.877
Our sympathies have been appealed to.

1093
01:00:16.957 --> 01:00:22.397
A great deal has been said about
the accused being a good boy,

1094
01:00:22.477 --> 01:00:29.237
having gone to church and has a great
many respectable friends in his hometown.

1095
01:00:30.797 --> 01:00:36.597
Such appeals to our sympathies are
always made by a clever attorney

1096
01:00:36.677 --> 01:00:42.297
when there are no solid facts to defend

1097
01:00:42.377 --> 01:00:44.717
a man accused.

1098
01:00:45.537 --> 01:00:51.657
Now, for my part, I am very happy to
hear that he has a great many respectable

1099
01:00:51.737 --> 01:00:56.437
friends in his hometown and has
always gone to church on Sunday.

1100
01:00:56.517 --> 01:01:02.797
But I am horrified, as I know that
all of you must be, when we know that

1101
01:01:02.877 --> 01:01:08.737
he uses this cloak of respectability
to cover up his complicity in

1102
01:01:08.817 --> 01:01:10.957
robbery and murder.

1103
01:01:11.157 --> 01:01:15.477
Now, there are only two points
for us to remember in this case,

1104
01:01:15.557 --> 01:01:21.457
ladies and gentlemen, and these points
speak more strongly than anything which I may

1105
01:01:21.537 --> 01:01:22.537
say.

1106
01:01:22.937 --> 01:01:25.477
John Arlington is dead.

1107
01:01:25.597 --> 01:01:30.837
He was killed when he tried to
protect himself and his property.

1108
01:01:31.157 --> 01:01:33.117
That is the first fact.

1109
01:01:33.197 --> 01:01:37.377
And John Arlington's jewels were found
in the pocket of Hector McDonald's coat.

1110
01:01:37.457 --> 01:01:42.417
With these facts clearly before us,
gentlemen, it is not necessary for me to remind

1111
01:01:42.497 --> 01:01:43.857
you of your duty.

1112
01:01:43.937 --> 01:01:48.597
of the attempt that we are making to grind
out ruthlessly under the stern heel of

1113
01:01:48.677 --> 01:01:53.277
justice, the ugly breed of criminals that
are threatened the lives and safety of all

1114
01:01:53.357 --> 01:01:54.357
of us.

1115
01:01:54.997 --> 01:02:00.177
I shall leave all the emotionalism in
this case in the hands of a fairly able

1116
01:02:00.257 --> 01:02:02.904
attorney for the defense.
Here, look at this.

1117
01:02:04.117 --> 01:02:06.617
That's Mrs. O'Grady's
handwriting, but she isn't here.

1118
01:02:06.697 --> 01:02:10.109
Where did you get this? Why,
in my hand here, on the desk.

1119
01:02:10.597 --> 01:02:12.597
What are you going to do about it?

1120
01:02:13.557 --> 01:02:15.617
We've nothing to lose.

1121
01:02:16.657 --> 01:02:17.757
Your Honor.

1122
01:02:33.037 --> 01:02:36.557
I beg to ask for a postponement of
this case until tomorrow morning.

1123
01:02:36.637 --> 01:02:38.317
What? To produce new evidence.

1124
01:02:38.397 --> 01:02:39.277
Please, Horses, Your Honor.

1125
01:02:39.357 --> 01:02:44.057
I object. In a case where a man's life is
at stake, we cannot refuse any reasonable

1126
01:02:44.137 --> 01:02:45.257
request.

1127
01:02:45.417 --> 01:02:49.377
On what ground? I hope to be able
to produce the missing witness,

1128
01:02:49.457 --> 01:02:51.417
Mrs. O'Grady. I object, Your Honor.

1129
01:02:51.497 --> 01:02:54.957
I'm beginning to have my doubt
that there is such a person as Mrs.

1130
01:02:55.037 --> 01:02:57.377
O'Grady. Oh, yes, there is, Your Honor.

1131
01:03:00.057 --> 01:03:02.377
Cease this disorder in the court.

1132
01:03:02.757 --> 01:03:05.737
In order that the defense may
produce the missing witness,

1133
01:03:05.817 --> 01:03:10.597
Mrs. O'Grady, This court is adjourned
until 10 o'clock tomorrow morning.

1134
01:03:18.877 --> 01:03:24.237
Now, Mrs. O'Grady, what were
you doing on Christmas evening?

1135
01:03:24.597 --> 01:03:27.077
I was trimming a Christmas tree.

1136
01:03:27.437 --> 01:03:29.977
Was Hector MacDonald helping you?

1137
01:03:30.457 --> 01:03:31.837
Yes, he was.

1138
01:03:31.917 --> 01:03:35.564
And was there anyone else with
you trimming the Christmas tree

1139
01:03:37.137 --> 01:03:38.317
Why, yes.

1140
01:03:38.397 --> 01:03:40.337
My granddaughter, Rosie O'Grady.

1141
01:03:40.417 --> 01:03:44.057
And, well, we had put the baby to bed.

1142
01:03:44.137 --> 01:03:45.637
A boy or girl?

1143
01:03:45.717 --> 01:03:47.017
Yes, sir.

1144
01:03:48.197 --> 01:03:52.017
Oh, I mean, a boy, sir.

1145
01:03:52.317 --> 01:03:54.517
And how long were you both with Mr.

1146
01:03:54.597 --> 01:03:55.597
MacDonald?

1147
01:03:55.837 --> 01:03:57.157
Oh, it was...

1148
01:03:57.237 --> 01:03:59.937
it was past midnight when we finished.

1149
01:04:00.977 --> 01:04:03.037
Are you sure of that?

1150
01:04:03.817 --> 01:04:09.017
Oh, yes, I'm quite positive I heard the
clock strike 12 while we were all there.

1151
01:04:09.097 --> 01:04:11.477
That's all. One moment, please.

1152
01:04:11.937 --> 01:04:13.777
As far as I'm concerned.

1153
01:04:13.937 --> 01:04:15.937
Oh, dear, is there some noise?

1154
01:04:16.017 --> 01:04:18.037
Yes, one or two questions.

1155
01:04:19.397 --> 01:04:24.577
Now, there is another member of your
family who is also hard to locate.

1156
01:04:24.657 --> 01:04:27.097
This big man, your son, I believe.

1157
01:04:27.177 --> 01:04:29.997
My son-in-law, the baby's father.

1158
01:04:30.077 --> 01:04:31.077
Oh, yes.

1159
01:04:32.537 --> 01:04:34.361
that evening trimming the tree?

1160
01:04:34.737 --> 01:04:36.117
Well, no.

1161
01:04:36.197 --> 01:04:38.097
Well, was he in bed too?

1162
01:04:39.257 --> 01:04:40.977
I think so.

1163
01:04:41.057 --> 01:04:43.577
You see, I don't put him to bed.

1164
01:04:44.897 --> 01:04:45.917
Oh,

1165
01:04:47.717 --> 01:04:49.677
now you are moaning around again.

1166
01:04:49.877 --> 01:04:51.377
Why the acts were scared of Mrs.

1167
01:04:51.457 --> 01:04:53.017
Eccles going to town?

1168
01:04:53.117 --> 01:04:53.897
What?

1169
01:04:53.977 --> 01:04:55.057
I'm not.

1170
01:04:55.217 --> 01:04:56.997
When did he say get back?

1171
01:04:57.077 --> 01:05:00.297
Say, Rosie, what's the
difference when he comes back?

1172
01:05:00.377 --> 01:05:02.977
But what are you worrying about him for?

1173
01:05:03.057 --> 01:05:05.477
I'm not worried about him, only...

1174
01:05:06.097 --> 01:05:10.937
the way you look at me, you
and that horrible little Midge.

1175
01:05:11.377 --> 01:05:13.217
You give me the creeps.

1176
01:05:13.297 --> 01:05:14.197
Yeah?

1177
01:05:14.277 --> 01:05:18.097
Well, no wonder. The Midge
wanted me to bump you up and echo.

1178
01:05:18.757 --> 01:05:20.717
Then split two ways with him.

1179
01:05:20.797 --> 01:05:21.797
I don't believe it.

1180
01:05:21.877 --> 01:05:23.857
I don't believe he could be that rotten.

1181
01:05:23.937 --> 01:05:25.777
He ain't any rottener than echo.

1182
01:05:25.857 --> 01:05:27.877
Neither one of them got any principles.

1183
01:05:27.957 --> 01:05:31.717
Now, if you have any
sense, you duck with me.

1184
01:05:32.057 --> 01:05:34.577
You're asking me to run away with you?

1185
01:05:34.757 --> 01:05:35.757
Yes.

1186
01:05:36.137 --> 01:05:37.877
I'm crazy about you.

1187
01:05:37.957 --> 01:05:40.517
While Echo is gone,
we have got our chance.

1188
01:05:40.597 --> 01:05:42.397
We tie up the midge and beat it.

1189
01:05:42.477 --> 01:05:44.637
Then you and I will split the stock.

1190
01:05:44.717 --> 01:05:46.437
Oh, beat yourself!

1191
01:06:36.277 --> 01:06:38.257
Come on!

1192
01:07:06.457 --> 01:07:07.337
Stop!

1193
01:07:07.417 --> 01:07:08.217
Wait!

1194
01:07:08.297 --> 01:07:09.297
Stop!

1195
01:07:09.757 --> 01:07:10.517
Stop!

1196
01:07:10.597 --> 01:07:11.157
Wait!

1197
01:07:11.237 --> 01:07:12.237
Take me away!

1198
01:07:12.317 --> 01:07:13.517
Take me away!

1199
01:07:13.597 --> 01:07:15.137
Don't go away without me!

1200
01:07:15.217 --> 01:07:16.497
Take me away!

1201
01:07:16.857 --> 01:07:19.337
Mrs. O'Bretty, you don't
know where your son-in-law is.

1202
01:07:19.417 --> 01:07:21.237
You don't know where your
granddaughter Rosie is.

1203
01:07:21.317 --> 01:07:24.437
Or your darling baby great
grandchild is, do you?

1204
01:07:24.517 --> 01:07:28.217
No, sir. But you remember perfectly well
every detail of what happened on Christmas

1205
01:07:28.297 --> 01:07:29.557
Eve four months ago.

1206
01:07:29.637 --> 01:07:31.437
Yes, sir. You remember trimming the tree.

1207
01:07:31.517 --> 01:07:36.097
But you don't remember anything else except
that you were on some mysterious farm in

1208
01:07:36.177 --> 01:07:37.897
the country. In short, Mrs.

1209
01:07:37.977 --> 01:07:42.877
O'Grady, you don't remember anything
else except what you want to remember,

1210
01:07:42.957 --> 01:07:43.717
do you?

1211
01:07:43.797 --> 01:07:45.877
Oh, I have such a headache.

1212
01:07:55.437 --> 01:07:56.997
Well, I'm sorry, Mrs.

1213
01:07:57.077 --> 01:07:59.177
O'Grady, if you have a headache, I...

1214
01:07:59.257 --> 01:08:00.157
Thank you.

1215
01:08:00.237 --> 01:08:02.337
I didn't mean to make you nervous.

1216
01:08:03.617 --> 01:08:07.117
You see, I'm only attempting
to drive her the truth.

1217
01:08:07.197 --> 01:08:09.217
Yes, of course. Now, Mrs.

1218
01:08:09.297 --> 01:08:10.297
O'Grady.

1219
01:08:11.217 --> 01:08:12.317
See, Your Honor?

1220
01:08:12.397 --> 01:08:13.797
Kitty Puffer, an Oscar.

1221
01:08:13.877 --> 01:08:15.957
Order! Order in the court!

1222
01:08:16.697 --> 01:08:18.717
What is the meaning of this?

1223
01:08:18.857 --> 01:08:21.504
Your Honor, I wish to
make a full convention.

1224
01:08:23.017 --> 01:08:24.397
After all, Nathan.

1225
01:08:24.477 --> 01:08:26.597
Five years isn't so long.

1226
01:08:26.737 --> 01:08:27.737
Hey,

1227
01:08:27.957 --> 01:08:30.545
one to five years.
Don't forget that, Rosie.

1228
01:08:30.717 --> 01:08:33.541
I'll be out of the old
joint before you know it.

1229
01:08:33.717 --> 01:08:35.177
I'm a good person.

1230
01:08:35.857 --> 01:08:37.557
I'm a good person.

1231
01:08:38.217 --> 01:08:40.697
You better make this snappy.

1232
01:08:40.777 --> 01:08:42.177
We've only got a minute.

1233
01:08:42.257 --> 01:08:43.377
All right, Chief.

1234
01:08:43.817 --> 01:08:46.237
I just want to tell you that
I appreciate what you did.

1235
01:08:46.317 --> 01:08:47.597
It was a big thing.

1236
01:08:48.097 --> 01:08:49.717
That's all right. Forget it, kid.

1237
01:08:49.797 --> 01:08:51.797
No, I'll never forget it.

1238
01:08:52.757 --> 01:08:55.277
I guess Rosie wants to talk to you now.

1239
01:08:55.357 --> 01:08:56.677
So I'll say goodbye.

1240
01:08:57.017 --> 01:08:58.877
Goodbye, kid. Good luck.

1241
01:09:00.377 --> 01:09:02.142
I brought you some cigarettes.

1242
01:09:03.437 --> 01:09:05.157
Well, thanks, kid.

1243
01:09:06.097 --> 01:09:08.417
Well, goodbye, Rosie.

1244
01:09:08.977 --> 01:09:10.297
Goodbye, Hector.

1245
01:09:11.797 --> 01:09:12.797
So long.

1246
01:09:15.977 --> 01:09:17.817
Good guy, huh?

1247
01:09:17.917 --> 01:09:18.917
Yes.

1248
01:09:21.757 --> 01:09:23.137
Well, Echo,

1249
01:09:23.357 --> 01:09:25.697
when you do come out, I'll...

1250
01:09:25.917 --> 01:09:27.597
I'll be waiting for you.

1251
01:09:28.897 --> 01:09:30.177
What, sir?

1252
01:09:30.797 --> 01:09:32.897
I'll be waiting for you.

1253
01:09:35.137 --> 01:09:37.257
I'm sorry. Are you on the level?

1254
01:09:38.217 --> 01:09:40.457
Do you really... Do you really want me...

1255
01:09:40.537 --> 01:09:41.717
Want me back?

1256
01:09:41.797 --> 01:09:42.937
Sure.

1257
01:09:44.397 --> 01:09:46.077
Oh, Rosie.

1258
01:09:48.057 --> 01:09:49.857
Gee, that's swell.

1259
01:09:50.717 --> 01:09:52.257
Well, say,

1260
01:09:52.477 --> 01:09:54.397
you came through like...

1261
01:09:54.477 --> 01:09:57.337
Like I asked you to and...

1262
01:09:57.757 --> 01:10:00.797
Well... I'll come through too.

1263
01:10:02.157 --> 01:10:04.297
A bargain, but...

1264
01:10:04.377 --> 01:10:05.977
A bargain?

1265
01:10:09.177 --> 01:10:10.237
Yeah.

1266
01:10:12.617 --> 01:10:13.857
Sure it is.

1267
01:10:17.677 --> 01:10:19.917
Rosie, I can't do that.

1268
01:10:20.057 --> 01:10:21.357
What do you mean?

1269
01:10:21.437 --> 01:10:24.317
Well, when a girl waits
for a fellow that long,

1270
01:10:24.657 --> 01:10:26.397
she's got to marry him.

1271
01:10:27.057 --> 01:10:31.417
And, well... Well, I just don't
want another ball and chain,

1272
01:10:31.497 --> 01:10:32.497
that's all.

1273
01:10:33.297 --> 01:10:34.997
You mean...

1274
01:10:35.177 --> 01:10:37.217
You mean you don't
want me to wait for you?

1275
01:10:37.297 --> 01:10:38.297
No.

1276
01:10:38.997 --> 01:10:40.897
You mean that, Echo?

1277
01:10:40.977 --> 01:10:42.797
Sure, I mean it.

1278
01:10:43.737 --> 01:10:44.737
Oh!

1279
01:10:45.257 --> 01:10:47.577
Oh, gee, Echo!

1280
01:10:47.997 --> 01:10:49.097
Oh!

1281
01:10:49.697 --> 01:10:52.377
Oh, you're a great guy!

1282
01:10:54.697 --> 01:10:57.037
I don't know what to say!

1283
01:10:59.497 --> 01:11:01.977
Hey, little girl. Don't get up, girl.

1284
01:11:03.757 --> 01:11:05.197
What did you say?

1285
01:11:05.277 --> 01:11:06.777
I didn't say nothing.

1286
01:11:13.737 --> 01:11:17.557
I don't know whether to laugh or cry.

1287
01:11:20.737 --> 01:11:23.357
Why don't you do a little of both?

1288
01:11:24.197 --> 01:11:26.077
You know the old gag.

1289
01:11:27.337 --> 01:11:29.357
That's all there is to life.

1290
01:11:29.637 --> 01:11:31.457
Just a little laugh.

1291
01:11:31.677 --> 01:11:33.337
A little tear.

1292
01:11:34.277 --> 01:11:35.277
More!

1293
01:11:36.397 --> 01:11:38.297
Say goodbye, Rosie. I'll be seeing you.

1294
01:11:38.377 --> 01:11:39.377
Come on.

1295
01:11:42.097 --> 01:11:43.317
Hey, you!

1296
01:11:43.597 --> 01:11:47.009
You'd better come over and
take care of this galley, or...

1297
01:11:47.357 --> 01:11:49.517
I'll send your postal card.

